<!-- 8. ABOUT SYSTEM -->
<h1 class="page-break">ABOUT SYSTEM</h1>
<h2>8.1 Introduction to CampusSync</h2>
<p><b>CampusSync</b> is an integrated Academic Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) platform designed specifically to automate collegiate administration, daily attendance logging, continuous internal evaluation, and statutory audit reporting. The system replaces obsolete manual rosters with an interconnected relational database, accessible through modern web browsers across desktops, tablets, and smartphones.</p>

<h2>8.2 Objectives of the System</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>Automate University Evaluation Scheme:</b> Calculate internal marks automatically using HNGU guidelines (best 2 out of 3 tests, assignments, active learning, attendance score, and practical components) without human error.</li>
    <li><b>Statutory Attendance Compliance:</b> Enable faculty to record daily lecture attendance in under 30 seconds and flag students with &lt;75% attendance to prevent detention risks.</li>
    <li><b>Instant Marksheet Delivery:</b> Allow students to view verified internal mark breakdowns and download tamper-proof official PDF mark cards instantly.</li>
    <li><b>Institutional Audit Intelligence:</b> Produce executive-level reports on demand, including pass/fail ratios, grade distributions, merit topper rankers, and division-level comparisons.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8.3 Scope of the System</h2>
<p>The scope encompasses the full semester lifecycle of undergraduate programs: Student enrollment and division management, faculty teaching allocation, lecture-by-lecture attendance logging, continuous internal marks assessment, result compilation, and final semester audit reporting.</p>

