<!-- 9. CURRENT MANUAL SYSTEM -->
<h1 class="page-break">CURRENT MANUAL SYSTEM VS. PROPOSED SYSTEM</h1>
<h2>9.1 Problems in the Existing Manual System</h2>
<p>The traditional system relies heavily on manual ledgers and standalone spreadsheets. This presents multiple administrative bottlenecks:</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Tedious Attendance Compilation:</b> Calculating end-of-semester attendance percentages manually across subjects takes days of administrative effort.</li>
    <li><b>Formula & Averaging Errors:</b> Calculating test averages, attendance marks, and internal totals by hand often leads to arithmetic mistakes.</li>
    <li><b>Data Insecurity & Privacy Leaks:</b> Paper marksheets posted on notice boards reveal every student's grades publicly.</li>
    <li><b>Delayed Defaulter Identification:</b> Students only discover they have attendance shortages right before final examinations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9.2 Proposed Solution (CampusSync ERP)</h2>
<p>CampusSync provides a unified, web-based platform with role-based dashboards. Attendance and marks are recorded once by faculty and immediately computed in real-time, eliminating calculation errors and providing instant transparency.</p>

<h2>9.3 Comparative Analysis Table</h2>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%; text-align: left;">Operational Criteria</th>
            <th style="width: 35%; text-align: left;">Legacy Manual / Excel Approach</th>
            <th style="width: 35%; text-align: left;">CampusSync Automated ERP</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><b>Data Repository</b></td><td>Physical registers & personal Excel files</td><td>Centralized MySQL relational database</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Attendance Processing</b></td><td>Days of manual counting at term end</td><td>Instant automated computation per lecture</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Internal Assessment</b></td><td>Prone to human addition & averaging errors</td><td>Strict algorithmic calculation via Python</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Result Publication</b></td><td>Paper sheets on notice boards</td><td>Secure password-protected student accounts</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Defaulter Warning System</b></td><td>Late paper notices at semester end</td><td>Live color-coded alerts (&lt;75% and &lt;85%)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Document Generation</b></td><td>Retyped marksheets & paper certificates</td><td>One-click official PDF with crest & seal</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Data Security & Backup</b></td><td>Risk of fire, wear, accidental deletion</td><td>Role-based authentication & encrypted passwords</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Audit Efficiency</b></td><td>Extensive manual preparation for inspections</td><td>Instant 2-page Executive Master PDF</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<div class="caption">Table 9.1: Comparative Analysis between Manual System and CampusSync ERP</div>
<div class="page-number-arabic">Page 6</div>

<!-- 10. TECHNOLOGY USED -->
<h1 class="page-break">TECHNOLOGY USED</h1>
<h2>10.1 Front-End Technologies</h2>
<p>The user interface is built using HTML5 for structure, Vanilla CSS3 for modern styling (custom variables, responsive Grid, Flexbox, glassmorphism), JavaScript (ES6+) for dynamic DOM interactions and fetch API requests, and Bootstrap 5.3 for responsive layouts.</p>

<h2>10.2 Back-End Framework</h2>
<p>The server application is built using Python 3.10 and the Flask framework. Flask organizes logic using modular Blueprints (auth, admin, faculty, student), and secures user credentials using scrypt hashing.</p>

<h2>10.3 Database Management System</h2>
<p>Data persistence is managed by MySQL Server 8.0, interacting through Flask-SQLAlchemy Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) and the PyMySQL connector.</p>

<h2>10.4 PDF & Document Generation</h2>
<p>Official documents are dynamically generated using ReportLab 3.x (with custom numbered canvas) and OpenPyXL for Excel batch imports and exports.</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 25%; text-align: left;">Architectural Tier</th>
            <th style="width: 35%; text-align: left;">Selected Technology</th>
            <th style="width: 40%; text-align: left;">Architectural Rationale</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><b>User Interface</b></td><td>HTML5, Vanilla CSS3, JS, Bootstrap 5.3</td><td>Fast page load times, responsive mobile view, zero bloat</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Application Layer</b></td><td>Python 3.10, Flask Framework</td><td>Rapid development, modular architecture, robust libraries</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Persistence Layer</b></td><td>MySQL 8.0 with SQLAlchemy ORM</td><td>Enterprise reliability, relational integrity, ACID compliance</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Document Processing</b></td><td>ReportLab & OpenPyXL</td><td>Automated vector PDF output and Excel file processing</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<div class="caption">Table 10.1: Technology Stack and Architectural Rationale</div>
